---
/**
 * @file mi-cuenta/comercio/nuevo/index.astro
 * @description Permanent redirect to `/{lang}/mi-cuenta/publica/`, the
 * in-account publish hub (HOS-1156 D-6, retargeted by HOS-2602).
 *
 * ## What was here
 *
 * A two-card vertical picker: gastronomía or experiencia, each linking to
 * `[vertical].astro`'s create form. The three publish pages are the picker now
 * — the header's "Publicar" menu offers all three verticals, and each one leads
 * straight to its own form rather than to a page that asks which form you meant.
 *
 * The picker's own copy (`listing.owner.create.pickVertical.*`) is retired with
 * it; nothing else reads those keys.
 *
 * A signed-in venue/experience owner who presses "+ Nuevo comercio" on
 * `/mi-cuenta/comercio/` is NOT sent here — that button goes to
 * `/mi-cuenta/publica/`, the hub that lists all three verticals and knows which
 * ones the account already holds. This 301 is for old inbound links.
 *
 * ## Why the hub and not `/publicar/` (HOS-2602)
 *
 * D-6 first pointed this URL at `/publicar/`, the ACCOMMODATION publish page. But
 * this URL names no vertical, and "comercio" is a venue or an experience — never
 * an accommodation — so a venue owner following an old link landed on «Nombre del
 * alojamiento». The URL cannot say which of the two it meant, so it goes where
 * "+ Nuevo comercio" goes: the hub that offers each vertical's own form. The
 * per-vertical child (`[vertical].astro`) already lands on the matching publish
 * page and is unchanged.
 *
 * @route     /{lang}/mi-cuenta/comercio/nuevo/
 * @rendering SSR (prerender=false) — emits a 301 and no body.
 */

import { buildPricingRedirectTarget } from '@/lib/pricing-redirect';
import { ACCOUNT_PUBLISH_HUB_PATH } from '@/lib/publish/publish-page-paths';

export const prerender = false;

const locale = Astro.locals.locale;

return Astro.redirect(
    buildPricingRedirectTarget({
        locale,
        path: ACCOUNT_PUBLISH_HUB_PATH,
        search: Astro.url.search
    }),
    301
);
---
